;; data/datascript-tx.edn — DataScript tx-data for the FTI catalog
;; (ADR-2607141700). Same shape as the sibling -9411-* files.
;;
;; THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the catalog. Two other files restate
;; it and are checked against it by the suite:
;;
;;   src/association/facts.kotoba   the Clojure-shaped reading (a literal map)
;;   src/association_facts.kotoba   the Kotoba port, GENERATED by
;;                                  scripts/gen_kotoba_port.cljs
;;
;; Before 2026-09-11 this catalog held two entries, both cited to
;; en.wikipedia.org, because the tick that seeded it recorded that
;; "fti.or.th's own domain rendered successfully but did not surface
;; founding-history detail on the pages checked". That was measured again on
;; 2026-09-11 and is FALSE: https://fti.or.th/AboutUs/background serves the
;; founding history, the statutory basis, the membership classes and the nine
;; statutory objectives, server-rendered. What the earlier check missed is
;; that fti.or.th is a Next.js site whose longest prose lives in the
;; __NEXT_DATA__ payload rather than in the rendered markup, so a reader that
;; strips tags and looks at the visible text alone sees the headings and not
;; the history. Every entry below carries the marker string that was found on
;; the page it cites; scripts/verify_citations.cljk re-fetches each URL and
;; refuses unless the marker is still there.
;;
;; The one-day disagreement between the Royal Gazette date FTI publishes
;; (28 December 1987) and the upgrade date Wikipedia/Wikidata publish
;; (29 December 1987) is recorded as two entries, not reconciled into one.
;; Thai acts commonly take effect the day after promulgation, which would make
;; both true, but this catalog has no source that says so for THIS act and
;; will not supply the inference itself.

